# Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the mod folder as it stands
# on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in Mod/ is published if the in-game button is
# used. Publishing goes through the CI, which ships the tracked files of Mod/ only; ignoring a file
# here keeps it out of that payload and out of git, not out of a folder uploaded straight from disk.

# Development environments
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings.
.claude/

# System
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Windows folder icons. Local derivatives of Mod/About/ModIcon.png and Mod/About/Preview.png for the
# Explorer (desktop.ini points at them); regenerable, never content, and never to be placed in Mod/.
*.ico

# RimWorld converts every PNG to a .dds next to it the first time the game loads the mod. They are
# a per-machine cache, regenerated on demand, and are not read again in a diff. None has ever been
# committed here; the pattern keeps it that way.
*.dds
*.DDS

# Test evidence: kept ON DISK for the session that reads it, not carried by the repository. Reports,
# captures and Player.log grow without bound (PickleTools saw 10 GB in a day). What is worth keeping
# in git is one short text line per run in docs/runs/, cited by STATUS.md. What to keep on disk, and
# what to delete, is written in TESTING.md ("Evidence to keep").
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/

# Outputs of the preview scripts (Art/render-preview.cjs, Art/check-contrast.py). They prove the
# Preview at the moment it was rendered and are rewritten by the next render; the scripts and their
# inputs (preview.html, preview-palette.json, Preview-source.png) are what is versioned.
Art/preview-background.png
Art/preview-thumbnail.png
Art/preview-contrast.json
Art/preview-render.json

# Build intermediates of the Pickle step assembly (Tests/Pickle/Source/Directory.Build.props sends them here, outside
# the test mod folder: the staging copies that folder as it is).
.build/

# The Pickle step assembly is a build artefact of the test companion mod, rebuilt with
# `dotnet build Tests/Pickle/Source/FunnyCreatures.PickleSteps.csproj -c Release` before a run and read from this folder by
# the WSL staging. It stays on disk, never in git. Mod/ is the Workshop payload and holds no assembly.
Tests/Pickle/Mod/Pickle/Assemblies/
